# The build context for Dockerfile.backend is the repository root, and Docker
# sends all of it to the builder before the Dockerfile picks anything out. So
# this file decides what can EVER reach an image layer.
#
# Deny everything, then allow back only what the API image copies. A new file
# anywhere in the repo is excluded until somebody adds it here on purpose.
*

!backend/requirements.txt
!backend/app/
!db/migrate.py
!db/provision_api_role.py
!db/migrations/

# Re-excluded inside the allowed folders. backend/.env holds real credentials;
# the rest is machine-specific.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
